    "description": "A named type is a type with a single name. This means native types, such as ``never``, ``int`` or ``array`` and custom types, such as classes and interfaces. It actually exclude constructed types, such as union types and intersection types. And DNF is included in union types.\n\nNamed types have a related Reflection class: ``ReflectionNamedType``.",
